          <li><BrandMark name={a.app} /><span>{a.app}</span><b>{pc(a.volume_share, 1)}</b></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <div class="grid">
        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 11 · Who captures the value"
          title={`Two apps intermediate ${(top2 * 100).toFixed(0)}% of India's transactions, and both sit above the ${(structure.cap * 100).toFixed(0)}% cap`}
          subtitle={`${structure.month}. Column width is share of transactions, height is average ticket, so area is roughly rupees moved.`}
          source="NPCI UPI Ecosystem Statistics, per-application volume and value, transcribed 2026-08-21. Shares computed against the NPCI national monthly total."
          download="/data/chart_market_structure.csv"
          wide
        >
          <Marimekko apps={structure.apps} cap={structure.cap} month={structure.month} />
        </Figure>

        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 12 · The cap gap"
          title={`Complying would move ${capMoveBn.toFixed(1)} billion transactions a month between apps`}
          subtitle={`Share of national UPI volume by app. The dashed line is the ${(structure.cap * 100).toFixed(0)}% cap; panels that breach it are marked.`}
          source="NPCI UPI Ecosystem Statistics and NPCI monthly product statistics."
          download="/data/chart_share_trend.csv"
          wide
        >
          <SmallMultiples months={shareTrend.months} series={shareTrend.series} reference={shareTrend.cap} />
        </Figure>

        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 13 · Share shift"
          title="The leaders have barely moved; the challengers started from nothing"
          subtitle="Share of national UPI volume, first period against latest."
          source="NPCI UPI Ecosystem Statistics."
        download="/data/chart_share_trend.csv"
        >
          <Slopegraph series={slopeSeries} startLabel={shareTrend.months[0]} endLabel={shareTrend.months.at(-1)} />
        </Figure>

        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 14 · Concentration"
          title="Concentration is falling, nowhere near fast enough to matter by December"
          subtitle="Herfindahl-Hirschman Index on true national volume shares. Above 2,500 is 'highly concentrated' by most competition authorities."
          source="Computed from NPCI per-application data."
        download="/data/chart_hhi.csv"
        >
          <EChart id="c-hhi" option={optHhi} />
        </Figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap module" id="module-banking">
      <h2 class="section-head"><span>F</span> Banking health scan</h2>
      <ul class="entities" aria-label="Banks in the two cohorts">
        {marketView.tickers.filter((t) => t.cohort !== 'Fintech').map((t) => (
          <li><BrandMark name={t.bank} tone={t.cohort === 'Private' ? 1 : 2} /><span>{t.bank}</span><b>{t.cohort}</b></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <div class="grid">
        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 15 · Cohort margins"
          title={`Private banks hold a ${Math.round(nim.gap_bps.at(-1)!)}bps margin advantage that has not closed`}
          subtitle="NIM proxy: net interest income over average total assets, computed from filed statements. The shaded band is the gap."
          source="Filed annual income statements and balance sheets, retrieved via yfinance. A proxy, not reported NIM. Banks use average earning assets, a smaller denominator."
        download="/data/chart_nim_slope.csv"
        >
          <SlopeLines periods={nim.periods} series={nim.series} gapBps={nim.gap_bps} />
        </Figure>

        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 16 · Margin decomposition"
          title="The advantage splits almost evenly between what banks earn and what they pay"
          subtitle={`FY${spread.fy}. Neither lever alone closes the gap, which is why it persists.`}
          source="Filed annual income statements and balance sheets, retrieved via yfinance."
        download="/data/chart_bank_spread.csv"
        >
          <EChart id="c-spread" option={optSpread} />
        </Figure>

        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 17 · Financial inclusion"
          title={`By ${incl.at(-1).year}, each banked adult was running ${incl.at(-1).txns_per_banked_adult_per_month} UPI transactions in an average month`}
          subtitle={`Up from ${incl[0].txns_per_banked_adult_per_month} in ${incl[0].year}. Access stopped being the constraint; intensity is the story, and the cost base.`}
          source="World Bank Findex account ownership (% of population 15+); the 15+ base is total population minus ages 0 to 14. UPI volume is the mean month of each year."
        download="/data/chart_inclusion.csv"
        >
          <EChart id="c-inclusion" option={optInclusion} />
        </Figure>

        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 18 · The market's verdict"
          title="The thinner-margin cohort massively outperformed: the franchise was already in the price"
          subtitle={`Median price return by cohort, ${marketView.window[0]} to ${marketView.window[1]}.`}
          source="Daily closes via yfinance. Price return only, and it excludes dividends, which understates the higher-yielding public cohort."
        download="/data/chart_market_view_series.csv"
        >
          <EChart id="c-marketview" option={optMarketView} />
        </Figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap module" id="module-diligence">
      <h2 class="section-head"><span>G</span> Private equity diligence simulation</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 19 · Unit economics"
          title={`${(unit.merchants / 1e6).toFixed(1)} million merchants, ${inr(unit.gmv_per_merchant_quarter_inr)} of GMV each per quarter, ₹0 of payment revenue`}
          subtitle={`Each merchant runs ${Math.round(unit.txns_per_merchant_quarter)} transactions a quarter. The bars show what one merchant would be worth per year if an MDR existed.`}
          source={SOURCE_PULSE}
          download="/data/chart_unit_economics.csv"
          wide
        >
          <EChart id="c-unit" option={optUnit} height={280} />
        </Figure>
      </div>
      <p class="callout">
        <strong>The recommendation:</strong> conditional no on a payments-fee thesis, conditional
        yes on merchant financing. The payment is the acquisition channel; the loan is the P&amp;L.
        <a href="/insights/diligence-merchant-payments">Read the diligence memo and its ambiguity register →</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap module" id="module-survey">
      <h2 class="section-head"><span>H</span> Survey analytics</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 20 · Episode-level NPS"
          title="One brand contains both the best and the worst episode in the market"
          subtitle="Scored per customer episode rather than per brand. A blended brand NPS averages these opposites into a number that hides the problem."
          source="SYNTHETIC panel of 2,000 respondents generated from a documented, seeded model (analysis/04_survey_nps.py). The method is the artefact; the figures illustrate it and are not market fact."
          download="/data/chart_nps_episodes.csv"
          wide
        >
          <div class="synthetic-flag">Synthetic data: illustrates the method, not the market</div>
          <EChart id="c-nps" option={optNps} height={300} />
        </Figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap module" id="module-geo">
      <h2 class="section-head"><span>I</span> Geographic gap</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 21 · One spends, one sends"
          title={`${mHigh.state} runs ${pc(mHigh.merchant_volume_share, 0)} of its transactions through merchants; ${mLow.state} runs ${pc(mLow.merchant_volume_share, 0)}`}
          subtitle={`Merchant share is measured from each state's own category split, not inferred from ticket size. Red is above the national ${pc(natMerchant, 0)}; bubble size is share of national transactions; states under ${(MIN_STATE * 100).toFixed(0)}% are omitted.`}
          source={SOURCE_PULSE + ' Per-state category files, reconciled against the country file at a ratio of 1.000000. A composition measure, not per-capita: no population denominator is invented.'}
          download="/data/chart_state_gap.csv"
          wide
        >
          <EChart id="c-states" option={optStates} height={340} />
        </Figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap module" id="module-wealth">
      <h2 class="section-head"><span>J</span> Wealth and asset management</h2>
      <Figure
        kicker="Exhibit 22 · The fund shelf"
        title={`${shelf.listed_schemes.toLocaleString('en-IN')} listed schemes are really ${shelf.distinct_strategies.toLocaleString('en-IN')} strategies`}
        subtitle={`Strip the Direct/Regular and Growth/IDCW wrappers and roughly ${Math.round((1 - shelf.distinct_strategies / shelf.listed_schemes) * 100)}% of the product count disappears. Counts schemes, not rupees.`}
        source={`AMFI daily NAV file, ${shelf.nav_date}. ${shelf.caveat}`}
        download="/data/chart_fund_shelf_by_asset_class.csv"
        wide
      >
        <EChart id="c-shelf" option={optShelf} height={320} />
      </Figure>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap module" id="module-pix">
      <h2 class="section-head"><span>K</span> The only comparable rail</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 23 · Same shape, twice"
          title="Both rails put the transactions in the merchant leg and the money somewhere else"
          subtitle={`Each bar is a leg's share of its own country's total, so nothing is converted between currencies. India is ${pixShape.india_period} on PhonePe's book; Brazil is ${pixShape.brazil_month}, national.`}
          source="Banco Central do Brasil, Pix open data, and PhonePe Pulse. Computed by analysis/09_pix_comparator.py."
          download="/data/chart_pix_shape.csv"
          wide
        >
          <EChart id="c-pix-shape" option={optPixShape} height={280} />
        </Figure>

        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 24 · The migration"
          title={`Brazil's merchant leg went from ${(pixMigration.volume_share[0] * 100).toFixed(1)}% to ${(pixMigration.volume_share.at(-1)! * 100).toFixed(1)}% of the rail with no price to attract it`}
          subtitle={`Monthly since Pix launched, on a time axis. The dashed line is India's merchant share of transactions in ${pixMigration.india_period}. The value line barely moves, which is the point.`}
          source="Banco Central do Brasil, Pix open data. Merchant is BCB's own P2B label, not derived."
          download="/data/chart_pix_migration.csv"
          wide
        >
          <EChart id="c-pix-migration" option={optPixMigration} height={300} />
        </Figure>

        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 25 · What was built on top"
          title={`Six years on, everything layered on the free rail is ${(pixProducts.add_on_share * 100).toFixed(2)}% of merchant transactions`}
          subtitle={`Recurring debits, open-finance initiation and contactless, each as a share of Brazil's merchant-leg volume. A layer reads null before it launched, never zero. Dynamic QR, which is distribution rather than revenue, is ${(pixProducts.dynamic_qr_share * 100).toFixed(0)}% and off this scale.`}
          source="Banco Central do Brasil, Pix open data, initiation method within the P2B leg."
          download="/data/chart_pix_products.csv"
          wide
        >
          <EChart id="c-pix-products" option={optPixProducts} height={300} />
        </Figure>

        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 26 · The disclosure gap"
          title="Brazil publishes instant-payment fraud every month; India publishes no machine-readable equivalent"
          subtitle={`Accepted fraud disputes per 100,000 transactions, and the share of disputed value returned. There is no Indian line to draw. The series ends ${pixFraud.latest_month}, four months behind the transaction table.`}
          source="Banco Central do Brasil, EstatisticasFraudesPix. India's losses are answered in Parliament on perimeters that do not line up with each other, which is why no comparable series is attempted."
          download="/data/chart_pix_fraud.csv"
          wide
        >
          <EChart id="c-pix-fraud" option={optPixFraud} height={300} />
        </Figure>
      </div>
      <p class="callout">
        <b>Why the comparator settles it:</b> the split this report opens with is not an
        artefact of India's zero-MDR statute. Brazil never had a discount rate to remove
        and arrived at the same shape, on a rail its central bank has had six years to
        monetise. What Brazil built on top is real and still {(pixProducts.add_on_share * 100).toFixed(2)}%
        of merchant transactions, which is an option rather than a business.
        <a href="/insights/pov-pix-comparator">Read the memo and what one comparator cannot show →</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap module" id="module-models">
      <h2 class="section-head"><span>L</span> What each model actually earns</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 27 · The margin ladder"
          title="The transaction business carries the most revenue and converts the least of it"
          subtitle={`Filed annual accounts, FY${bizRows[0].fy}. Bars are revenue, the line is net margin. Named companies rather than cohort averages, because two of the three groups hold a single company.`}
          source="Filed annual income statements via Yahoo Finance. Not like-for-like companies: different revenue recognition, perimeters and regulators, so only the shape of the margin each model produces is compared. Computed by analysis/10_business_models.py."
          download="/data/chart_business_models.csv"
          wide
        >
          <EChart id="c-biz-models" option={optBizModels} height={300} />
        </Figure>

        <Figure
          kicker="Exhibit 28 · How they got there"
          title="The rail took four years to reach a margin the others started above"
          subtitle="Net margin by fiscal year. A company reads null in a year it had not listed or did not report, never zero, so the lines break rather than bridge."
          source="Filed annual income statements via Yahoo Finance."
          download="/data/chart_margin_trajectory.csv"
          wide
        >
          <EChart id="c-margin-trail" option={optMarginTrail} height={300} />
        </Figure>
      </div>
      <p class="callout">
        <b>This is the recommendation, audited:</b> the report has argued since section A
        that the business is distribution rather than transactions. The only listed
        transaction business earns the thinnest margin in the panel, and the depository,
        which is plumbing everyone must cross and <i>is</i> allowed to charge for it, earns
        the widest. The difference between those two is not scale. It is price.
        <a href="/insights/pov-business-models">Read the memo and what four companies cannot show →</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap module" id="workbench">
      <h2 class="section-head"><span>M</span> Analyst workbench</h2>
      <Figure
        kicker="Interactive · Client-ready dashboard"
        title="Every state's payment mix, three linked ways, without leaving the page"
        subtitle="A tile cartogram, a sortable table and a detail panel, all linked: select in one and the others follow. Metric switch, live filter, no BI backend."
        source={SOURCE_PULSE}
        wide
      >
        <Workbench states={stateGap.states} period={stateGap.period} />
      </Figure>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap module" id="gap-matrix">
      <h2 class="section-head"><span>N</span> Coverage and limits</h2>
      <Figure
        kicker="Scope"
        title="The areas this report does not cover are the ones that would change its conclusion"
        subtitle="A scan that only ever reports full coverage is not a scan. Every gap below says what is missing and why."
        source="Self-assessed against the question this report set out to answer. Coverage is judged on what is computed from data in this repository, never on what is asserted in prose."
        wide
      >
        <GapMatrix />
      </Figure>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap module" id="memos">
      <h2 class="section-head"><span>O</span> The memos</h2>
      <div class="memo-grid">
        {memos.map((m) => (
          <a href={`/insights/${m.id}`}>
            <span class="kicker">{MEMO_KICKER[m.id]}</span><b>{m.data.title}</b>
          </a>
        ))}
        <a href="/methodology"><span class="kicker">Method</span><b>Sources, provenance and what this analysis cannot know</b></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

